  "summary_en": "Sharpen sharpens a layer with an unsharp mask: a blurred negative of the source is combined with the original. The page marks the node as available since Houdini 21.0.",
  "inputs": [
    "source: the input layer or VDB to sharpen",
    "size (optional): per-pixel size amount, scaled by the Size parameter",
    "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount, scaled by the Mask parameter"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Signature: the layer type the source accepts",
    "Mask: how much of the new value mixes with the original (default 1, only the new value)",
    "Units: blur radius in Image space or Pixels",
    "Read Pixels outside Image: includes pixels beyond the image edge, according to the border type",
    "Size: radius of the sharpen effect; higher values give crisper results",
    "Scale Size: scales the sharpen radius",
    "Amplitude: strength of the unsharp mask",
    "Gain: multiplies the original brightness; Gain 0 with a positive Amplitude gives a high-pass filter",
    "Threshold: minimum pixel difference before sharpening occurs"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Sharpening can introduce black edges; the suggested fix is a Maximum node with the original layer on bg and the Sharpen filter output on fg",
    "The page describes no other limitations"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Sharpen accentue une couche par masque flou : un négatif flouté de la source est combiné à l'original, ce qui durcit les contours."
